Subject: open: treat ENOENT from opening a directory like EACCES on OpenVMS

The VMS CRTL cannot open() a directory by its Unix name and reports ENOENT.
Use gnulib's existing REPLACE_OPEN_DIRECTORY fallback (dummy fd + registered
name, as on mingw) so that grep -r and fts work.

--- a/lib/open.c	2026-10-02 21:06:14.571370977 +0100
+++ b/lib/open.c	2026-10-02 21:06:14.590314907 +0100
@@ -158,7 +158,14 @@
      on Linux (ie. always reports EOF on attempts to read()), and
      override fstat() in fchdir.c to hide the fact that we have a
      dummy.  */
-  if (REPLACE_OPEN_DIRECTORY && fd < 0 && errno == EACCES
+  /* OpenVMS: open() of a directory by its Unix name ("dir", "dir/", ".")
+     fails with ENOENT, although stat() and opendir() succeed.  */
+# ifdef __VMS
+#  define OPEN_DIRECTORY_ERRNO(e) ((e) == EACCES || (e) == ENOENT)
+# else
+#  define OPEN_DIRECTORY_ERRNO(e) ((e) == EACCES)
+# endif
+  if (REPLACE_OPEN_DIRECTORY && fd < 0 && OPEN_DIRECTORY_ERRNO (errno)
       && ((flags & O_ACCMODE) == O_RDONLY
           || (O_SEARCH != O_RDONLY && (flags & O_ACCMODE) == O_SEARCH)))
     {
